WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.367
Multi-source workflows can execute tools sequentially, in parallel, or conditionally.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:11.712
Use sequential execution when the second tool needs a value from the first.

00:00:11.712 --> 00:00:17.507
For example, first identify an account, then request that account's history.

00:00:17.507 --> 00:00:21.507
Use parallel execution when the tools are independent.

00:00:21.507 --> 00:00:26.015
Policy search and order lookup may be able to run at the same time.

00:00:26.662 --> 00:00:32.429
Use conditional execution when the second source is only needed if the first is insufficient.

00:00:32.429 --> 00:00:41.189
For example, search an internal knowledge base first, and use public web search only if the application explicitly

00:00:41.189 --> 00:00:45.133
permits it and the task really requires current external information.

00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:51.410
A useful project question is: does tool B depend on tool A's output?

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:55.975
If not, parallel execution may reduce latency.

00:00:55.975 --> 00:00:59.289
If yes, keep the dependency explicit.
